From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <colum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: TF_DS_CACHE_METRICS=on publishes the memory cache's counters regardless of
 tier, a resume-depth histogram and the coarse counters' causes

The prompt cache's counters reach /health and /metrics only when a tier or grouping is on
(LaneHost.configure), so the default pair (SPILL_GIB=0) shows nothing to a hit-rate campaign;
misses/refused/evicted/failed each merge several causes and there is no resume-depth distribution
(review finding 12).

TF_DS_CACHE_METRICS (on by default, as TF_DS_ENGRAM_METRICS; 0 or off turns it off) publishes the
memory CacheStats regardless of tier (lane_host's publish from configure and start; engine_api's
CacheStats in Status), splits the coarse counters by cause at the branches that already distinguish
them (misses: no prefix / tail-window / stale, a cause raised only by an entry whose tokens
prefix-match the prompt; refused: budget / restores in flight; evicted:
superseded / LRU; failed: save / restore) and accumulates a per-pass resume-depth histogram
(0/25/50/75/90/99/100 percent of prompt tokens resumed) on /metrics and /health beside the existing
counters. Because the counters alone no longer imply a tier, Spill.unbound now reads a tier-bound
marker (CacheStats.tier_bound) instead of Status.cache nullness.

With the switch off (0 or off) the store counts neither the cause splits nor the depth, the detail is
absent and the output is byte-identical to base; the prompt cache: log line and
tensorfold:engram_lookup_seconds are untouched. The switch is per-rank observability only and needs
no rank-pair agreement; start.sh's TF_DS_* passthrough carries it unchanged.

Tests: zig build test and zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh pass; the patch's own tests: the "0"/"off"
parse, the metrics-off status test (nothing parked, no cache counters), the no-tier publishing
test, the miss/eviction/failure cause splits, the miss-cause attribution case (an entry longer
than the prompt raises no tail_window), the refused budget-vs-restores split, the
resume-depth buckets, the off-path no-counting test, and the render/health publishing tests. Not
run on a pair.
---
